  "rules": [
    "HP6+8/wave, contact1+0.6/wave, speed250+/-25px/s; HP factor1. Body29.0172px at0/10, hurt32px at total0/4, contact16.0312px at0/5.",
    "Before detection choose random goals in the source500+/-100px square around the target. Inclusive650px detection latches once, adds90px/s times accessibility and switches to direct two-axis following.",
    "Independent repeating1s Timer adds45px/s times accessibility, max10 boosts. The Timer keeps its phase while capped and through contact resets.",
    "New contact entry sets boost count and all native speed bonus to0; detection remains latched. Continuous overlap is not another entry. Contact maps use stable namespaced player identities/native enemy IDs so slot changes or faction transfer do not alias identities.",
    "Baby T-Rex alone retains its optional live-player speed cap. Normal Velociraptor has no such cap, no size/damage boost, no border clamp/player body mask, and no ++ warning charge."
  ],
  "interfaces": [
    "Enemies.NativeDetection={radius,speedBonus}; NativeTargetDetection owns the one-time latch, World.detections is a persistent transfer/compaction column.",
    "Pursuer.playerSpeedShare now optional; resetOnContact is source-driven. beginContacts/contact/endContacts reuse two per-actor maps without per-frame map allocation.",
    "World.step adds optional final targetKeys:{number|string}; ordinary EnemySim passes Player:UserId strings and CharmedWorld passes native enemy IDs. Existing callers retain slot fallback.",
    "Existing nativeChargeAccessibility callback also scales source flat detection/Pursuer bonuses; no new remote/schema/Arsenal interface."
  ],
